Yum!  This was the frosting for my daughter's first birthday cake (cake was Creay White Layers, filling was Lemon Filling-- both also on this site).  Wonderful, pretty, tasty frosting.  Here were my modifications, based on other reviews:
- I used 1 c. salted butter, 1 c. shortening, and omitted the salt; 
- I used only 4.5 cups of powdered sugar; 
- I used only 1/2 cup (4 oz.) heavy cream. 
Next time, I will only make 1/2 a recipe.  That would have been enough to liberally frost my filled 9-in. 2 layer cake.  I think it would be enough even if I were using this frosting to fill the cake.  Not that there's anything wrong with leftover frosting-- it's great with fresh strawberries and vanilla wafers!

Made these along withe Protestant Margaritas(lol)
for a get together of 12 og my friends & family,
9 gave the Catholic one 5 stars, 1gave it 3 & 2 gave it 41/2. I call it at 5 stars!
